<strong>What separates Tier 1 from Tier 5:</strong> Tier 1 cities average $6,055/month salary with 1.4% inflation; Tier 5 cities average $455/month with 28.4% inflation. The purchasing power index drops from 157.1 to 48.0 — a 3.3x gap. Paradoxically, Tier 1 has a <em>higher</em> rent-to-salary ratio (67.4%) than Tier 5 (53.6%), because extreme housing costs in affluent cities slightly outpace even their high salaries.
