<section id="inflation-oil-exposure">
<h2>5. Inflation and Oil Shock Exposure</h2>

<p>Inflation and oil dependency are key structural vulnerabilities. Cities with high oil shock exposure face an average inflation rate of 20.4% — six times that of low-exposure cities (3.4%). This correlation is driven by a cluster of conflict-affected, oil-dependent, and structurally fragile economies.</p>

